Job Description & Summary
At PwC, our people in data and analytics focus on leveraging data to drive insights and make informed business decisions. They utilise advanced analytics techniques to help clients optimise their operations and achieve their strategic goals. 

In data analysis at PwC, you will focus on utilising advanced analytical techniques to extract insights from large datasets and drive data-driven decision-making. You will leverage skills in data manipulation, visualisation, and statistical modelling to support clients in solving complex business problems. 

Why PWC&nbsp; 

At PwC, you will be part of a vibrant community of solvers that leads with trust and creates distinctive outcomes for our clients and communities. This purpose-led and values-driven work, powered by technology in an environment that drives innovation, will enable you to make a tangible impact in the real world. We reward your contributions, support your wellbeing, and offer inclusive benefits, flexibility programmes and mentorship that will help you thrive in work and life. Together, we grow, learn, care, collaborate, and create a future of infinite experiences for each other. Learn more about us&nbsp; 

At PwC, we believe in providing equal employment opportunities, without any discrimination on the grounds of gender, ethnic background, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, religion or other beliefs, perceived differences and status protected by law. We strive to create an environment where each one of our people can bring their true selves and contribute to their personal growth and the firm's growth. To enable this, we have zero tolerance for any discrimination and harassment based on the above considerations. "&nbsp; 

Responsibilities: 

We are seeking an experienced Azure DevOps Engineer to join our dynamic team immediately. The ideal candidate will have strong expertise in infrastructure deployment, container orchestration, and networking within Azure environments, with a focus on EKS and Kubernetes. This role requires hands-on experience with CloudFormation and deep knowledge of Azure networking concepts. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities: &nbsp; 

- 
Design, implement, and manage scalable and secure infrastructure using Azure CloudFormation. &nbsp; 

- 
Deploy and manage containerized applications using Amazon EKS and Kubernetes. &nbsp; 

- 
Configure and troubleshoot azure networking components including VPC, subnets, security groups, load balancers, and route tables. &nbsp; 

- 
Collaborate with development and operations teams to automate deployment pipelines and infrastructure provisioning. &nbsp; 

- 
Monitor, troubleshoot, and optimize cloud infrastructure and Kubernetes clusters. &nbsp; 

- 
Ensure security best practices and compliance in cloud infrastructure and deployments. &nbsp; 

- 
Maintain and improve CI/CD processes integrating with Azure and Kubernetes environments. &nbsp; 

Mandatory skill sets: &nbsp; 

- 
Strong expertise in Amazon EKS and Kubernetes management and troubleshooting. &nbsp; 

- 
Hands-on experience with Azure CloudFormation for infrastructure as code (IaC). &nbsp; 

- 
Strong networking knowledge including VPC, subnets, routing, and security groups within Azure. &nbsp; 

- 
Experience in infrastructure deployment and automation. &nbsp; 

- 
certifications related to DevOps, Kubernetes, or networking preferred. &nbsp; 

